1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,465
Four customers write to you.

2
00:00:02,465 --> 00:00:03,939
One sees bad gateway.

3
00:00:03,939 --> 00:00:05,974
One sees service unavailable.

4
00:00:05,974 --> 00:00:07,728
One sees gateway timeout.

5
00:00:07,728 --> 00:00:10,676
And one says the connection is not secure.

6
00:00:11,226 --> 00:00:12,624
Four different messages,

7
00:00:12,624 --> 00:00:13,905
four different causes.

8
00:00:13,905 --> 00:00:14,662
If you guess,

9
00:00:14,662 --> 00:00:15,651
you lose an hour.

10
00:00:15,651 --> 00:00:17,107
If you read the evidence,

11
00:00:17,107 --> 00:00:18,330
you lose two minutes.

12
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:22,528
Today you learn where each error leaves its evidence, and how to read it.

13
00:00:23,078 --> 00:00:24,230
Read the evidence.

14
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:28,852
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

15
00:00:29,402 --> 00:00:32,474
One: what each symptom means, and the place to look for it.

16
00:00:33,024 --> 00:00:37,845
Two: a live demo. One real engine X, with four faults at the same time.

17
00:00:38,395 --> 00:00:43,046
Three: we find each cause, in the error log, in the config, and in the certificate.

18
00:00:43,596 --> 00:00:44,919
Four: we fix all four,

19
00:00:44,919 --> 00:00:45,701
and prove it.

20
00:00:45,701 --> 00:00:46,603
Then your turn,

21
00:00:46,603 --> 00:00:49,249
with a lab that judges you with five checks.

22
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:52,685
This is lesson seven of the web servers domain.

23
00:00:52,685 --> 00:00:53,360
After this,

24
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,815
one mastery lesson ties it all together.

25
00:00:56,365 --> 00:00:57,517
Read the evidence.

26
00:00:59,567 --> 00:01:01,743
Four symptoms, four places to look.

27
00:01:02,293 --> 00:01:03,066
Five oh two,

28
00:01:03,066 --> 00:01:03,839
bad gateway.

29
00:01:03,839 --> 00:01:07,189
Engine X reached for the app and got nothing useful.

30
00:01:07,189 --> 00:01:12,085
The error log usually says connection refused: nothing listens on that port.

31
00:01:12,635 --> 00:01:13,471
Five oh four,

32
00:01:13,471 --> 00:01:14,500
gateway timeout.

33
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,171
The app is alive but slow.

34
00:01:16,171 --> 00:01:18,679
The error log says up stream timed out,

35
00:01:18,679 --> 00:01:21,958
and the config has a timeout shorter than the work.

36
00:01:22,508 --> 00:01:23,424
Five oh three,

37
00:01:23,424 --> 00:01:24,733
service unavailable.

38
00:01:24,733 --> 00:01:27,285
Often on purpose: a maintenance switch,

39
00:01:27,285 --> 00:01:28,005
or a limit.

40
00:01:28,005 --> 00:01:29,249
Look in the config,

41
00:01:29,249 --> 00:01:30,230
not in the app.

42
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:35,691
And a T L S error is not a status code at all: the handshake fails first.

43
00:01:35,691 --> 00:01:37,171
Check the certificate.

44
00:01:37,171 --> 00:01:37,776
Its name,

45
00:01:37,776 --> 00:01:38,449
its dates,

46
00:01:38,449 --> 00:01:39,122
its chain.

47
00:01:40,672 --> 00:01:45,856
Go to the lab folder.

48
00:01:47,406 --> 00:01:49,305
Look around. Type: L S.

49
00:01:49,855 --> 00:01:50,590
The config,

50
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:51,594
a probe script,

51
00:01:51,594 --> 00:01:52,865
a maintenance flag,

52
00:01:52,865 --> 00:01:54,604
a certificate and its key.

53
00:01:54,604 --> 00:01:55,674
Behind engine X,

54
00:01:55,674 --> 00:01:57,748
a small app is already running.

55
00:01:58,298 --> 00:02:02,351
Probe all four.

56
00:02:02,901 --> 00:02:03,836
Four requests,

57
00:02:03,836 --> 00:02:04,770
four failures.

58
00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:05,705
A five oh two,

59
00:02:05,705 --> 00:02:06,706
a five oh four,

60
00:02:06,706 --> 00:02:07,774
a five oh three,

61
00:02:07,774 --> 00:02:09,843
and a failed secure connection.

62
00:02:09,843 --> 00:02:11,712
Let us take them one by one.

63
00:02:12,262 --> 00:02:27,025
502: ask the error log.

64
00:02:27,575 --> 00:02:28,805
Connection refused,

65
00:02:28,805 --> 00:02:29,907
error one eleven.

66
00:02:29,907 --> 00:02:31,656
Engine X called an address,

67
00:02:31,656 --> 00:02:32,951
and nobody answered.

68
00:02:32,951 --> 00:02:34,700
So who is really listening?

69
00:02:35,250 --> 00:02:44,125
See what listens.

70
00:02:44,675 --> 00:02:45,989
Eighty-two forty-one,

71
00:02:45,989 --> 00:02:46,740
forty-three,

72
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:47,741
and forty-eight.

73
00:02:47,741 --> 00:02:49,368
The app is on forty-eight.

74
00:02:49,368 --> 00:02:51,245
Nothing listens on forty-nine.

75
00:02:51,795 --> 00:02:57,918
Find the port in the config.

76
00:02:58,468 --> 00:03:02,295
There it is: the proxy pass points at eighty-two forty-nine.

77
00:03:02,295 --> 00:03:03,316
One wrong digit.

78
00:03:03,316 --> 00:03:04,847
That is the five oh two.

79
00:03:05,397 --> 00:03:16,597
504: ask the error log.

80
00:03:17,147 --> 00:03:21,733
Up stream timed out. The app is alive, but engine X stopped waiting for it.

81
00:03:22,283 --> 00:03:27,937
Find the timeout.

82
00:03:28,487 --> 00:03:33,457
Proxy read timeout, one second. The report takes three. That is the five oh four.

83
00:03:34,007 --> 00:03:42,007
503: look in the config.

84
00:03:42,557 --> 00:03:44,099
This one is on purpose.

85
00:03:44,099 --> 00:03:47,117
If a file called maintenance dot flag exists,

86
00:03:47,117 --> 00:03:50,067
engine X answers five oh three for the shop.

87
00:03:50,617 --> 00:03:54,222
Is the flag there?

88
00:03:54,772 --> 00:03:57,865
Yes. Someone forgot to remove it after the last release.

89
00:03:58,415 --> 00:04:09,765
TLS: read the certificate name.

90
00:04:10,315 --> 00:04:15,883
Wrong dot example. The site is local host, so every client refuses this certificate.

91
00:04:16,433 --> 00:04:29,489
Write the three answers.

92
00:04:30,039 --> 00:04:33,132
Read them back. Type: cat, answers dot text.

93
00:04:33,682 --> 00:04:35,623
Three words, three diagnoses.

94
00:04:36,173 --> 00:04:41,528
Open the config in vim.

95
00:04:42,078 --> 00:04:43,247
Go to line fifteen,

96
00:04:43,247 --> 00:04:46,079
and change the port to eighty-two forty-eight.

97
00:04:46,079 --> 00:04:47,248
Then line eighteen,

98
00:04:47,248 --> 00:04:49,587
and change the timeout to ten seconds.

99
00:05:04,737 --> 00:05:09,047
Remove the flag.

100
00:05:09,597 --> 00:05:40,695
Make a new certificate.

101
00:05:41,245 --> 00:05:47,346
Test, then reload.

102
00:05:47,896 --> 00:05:49,624
Applied without stopping anything.

103
00:05:50,174 --> 00:05:53,481
Probe again.

104
00:05:54,031 --> 00:05:59,556
Two hundred, four times. Each fix matched its evidence, so each one worked the first time.

105
00:06:00,106 --> 00:06:02,474
Run the judge.

106
00:06:03,024 --> 00:06:03,808
Five checks.

107
00:06:03,808 --> 00:06:05,311
The four services work,

108
00:06:05,311 --> 00:06:08,185
and your three diagnoses match the evidence.

109
00:06:08,185 --> 00:06:09,296
Five out of five.

110
00:06:09,846 --> 00:06:11,809
Clean up.

111
00:06:12,359 --> 00:06:15,879
Engine X and the app are stopped, and everything is removed.

112
00:06:16,429 --> 00:06:24,855
Are the ports free? Count the lines.

113
00:06:25,405 --> 00:06:28,413
Zero. Nothing listens, nothing is left behind.

114
00:06:29,963 --> 00:06:34,912
Your task. Four things are broken. Find each cause from the evidence, then fix them.

115
00:06:35,462 --> 00:06:38,065
One: lab up, and probe. See four failures.

116
00:06:38,615 --> 00:06:42,284
Two: for the five oh two, read the error log, and see what listens.

117
00:06:42,834 --> 00:06:44,578
Three: for the five oh four,

118
00:06:44,578 --> 00:06:45,760
read the error log,

119
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:46,757
and the timeout.

120
00:06:46,757 --> 00:06:48,126
For the five oh three,

121
00:06:48,126 --> 00:06:49,745
find the maintenance flag.

122
00:06:49,745 --> 00:06:50,368
For T L S,

123
00:06:50,368 --> 00:06:51,986
read the certificate name.

124
00:06:52,536 --> 00:06:57,400
Four: write your three diagnoses into answers dot text, before you fix anything.

125
00:06:57,950 --> 00:06:59,219
Five: fix the port,

126
00:06:59,219 --> 00:07:00,019
the timeout,

127
00:07:00,019 --> 00:07:01,955
the flag and the certificate.

128
00:07:01,955 --> 00:07:02,422
Reload,

129
00:07:02,422 --> 00:07:02,823
probe,

130
00:07:02,823 --> 00:07:03,757
run lab check,

131
00:07:03,757 --> 00:07:04,692
then lab down.

132
00:07:06,742 --> 00:07:10,518
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen, and write it down.

